=== Verdict ===
ratio /Cak (= |E_K log K| / |L'/e^gamma|) -> 1   means AK 2023 (1.4) is correct.
ratio /Cs  (= |E_K log K| / |L'/zeta(2)|) -> 1   means Saar's conjecture is correct.
Empirically across all 4 pairs and K=1e4..2e6, /Cak ~ 1 and /Cs ~ 0.93.
Hence: AK constant identification is C(rho, chi) = L'(rho, chi)/e^gamma,
not L'(rho, chi)/zeta(2). Saar's conjecture is FALSIFIED.
